  "notes": "Epoch AI (epoch.ai/models/<slug>) publishes a per-model page for each tracked model with its own independently-run Epoch Capabilities Index (ECI) and benchmark scorecard (Chess Puzzles, Mystery Game Puzzles, Earthborne Rangers/EBR-bench, FrontierMath Erdos/Tiers 1-3/Tier 4 v2, GPQA Diamond, MirrorCode, OTIS Mock AIME, SimpleQA Verified, ARC-AGI-1/2, WeirdML v2, Vending-Bench 2, Text Arena Coding, SimpleBench) \u2014 a distinct third-party evaluation suite from the vendor launch tables and Artificial Analysis boards already in this pack, and not covered by the sibling boards/roster lanes (which checked the epoch.ai/models roster-listing page, not these per-model deep-dive pages). Pages are client-hydrated Astro (no usable static payload); rendered via headless browser (grab.py). For metric_ids that collide with existing vendor-table names (FrontierMath Tier 1-3/4 v2, GPQA Diamond, ARC-AGI-1/2), every row here is marked comparable:false with comparability_group 'epoch-ai-independent-2026-09' since Epoch runs its own harness/grading, not the vendor's -- per house convention (same id only for the same definition, cross-harness distinction via row-level comparable/comparability_group, not new ids). claude-opus-5-5, gpt-6-sol, and gpt-6-luna do not yet have Epoch AI per-model pages as of 2026-09-22 (HTTP 404, confirmed against the same URL pattern that resolves for all other rows here) -- recorded in missing[], not silently omitted.",
